From 417ad75a6f267e82ccd1e8e95696a1ac776bc1db Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MCC45TR <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 18:29:01 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: gdsc: preserve collapse write errors

Do not replace a failed collapse write with a successful status poll or
the votable power-off fast path. Keep resources held when the requested
transition is uncertain. Generic regulator and ICC retry accounting is
outside this change.

Signed-off-by: MCC45TR <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/clk/qcom/gdsc.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/qcom/gdsc.c b/drivers/clk/qcom/gdsc.c
index b99d701..b182ca2 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/gdsc.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/gdsc.c
@@ -162,6 +162,8 @@ static int gdsc_toggle_logic(struct gdsc *sc, enum gdsc_status status,
 	}
 
 	ret = gdsc_update_collapse_bit(sc, status == GDSC_OFF);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
 
 	/* If disabling votable gdscs, don't poll on status */
 	if ((sc->flags & VOTABLE) && status == GDSC_OFF && !wait) {
-- 
2.56.0

